n re-identification (Re-ID)': {'description': ['The task of identifying a specific person across different camera views or time instances.', 'Task for training person Re-ID task.'], 'type': ['task'], 'source_chunk_index': [0, 9]}, 'Scale-normalized image and feature pyramids (SIFP)': {'description': ['A paradigm that exploits scale-normalized image and feature pyramids to address the scale variation problem, improving both performance and speed.', 'A paradigm designed to handle scale variations in unified pose approaches.'], 'type': ['method'], 'source_chunk_index': [0, 12]}, 'ResNet-18': {'description': ['A convolutional neural network architecture used as a backbone in the experiments.', 'A smaller backbone network used in the pose estimation head.', 'A specific backbone network architecture used in the study.', 'A backbone model used in FastPose.'], 'type': ['method'], 'source_chunk_index': [0, 9, 10]}, 'pose estimation': {'description': ['The task of identifying and locating keypoints of a person in an image or video.', 'Task evaluated on COCO and PoseTrack datasets.', 'The task of determining the position of key body joints in an image or video.'], 'type': ['task'], 'source_chunk_index': [1, 12, 9]}, 'multi-person pose estimation': {'description': ['The task of estimating poses of multiple people in an image or video.'], 'type': ['task'], 'source_chunk_index': [1, 4]}, 'real-time inference': {'description': ['The ability of a system to perform inference quickly.', 'The ability of FastPose to perform pose tracking in real-time.'], 'type': ['task'], 'source_chunk_index': [1, 12]}, 'Multi-person pose estimation': {'description': ['The objective of estimating the poses of multiple people in a scene.', 'The task of estimating poses of multiple people.', 'The task of identifying and tracking the poses of multiple people in a video sequence over time.'], 'type': ['task'], 'source_chunk_index': [2, 4]}, 'Pose tracking': {'description': ['The task of tracking human poses across video frames.', 'The objective of tracking human poses in videos.', 'The task of tracking the pose of a person or object over time.', 'The objective of tracking human poses over time.', 'The task of tracking human poses across video frames, as described in the text.'], 'type': ['task'], 'source_chunk_index': [2, 3, 4, 9, 10, 12]}, 'Top-down pose estimation methods': {'description': ['A class of methods for pose estimation that first detect people and then estimate their poses.', 'Methods for pose estimation.', 'A method for human pose estimation that first detects the human bounding boxes and then estimates the pose within each box.'], 'type': ['method'], 'source_chunk_index': [2, 4]}, 'Flow-based pose similarity': {'description': ['A metric used to measure the similarity of poses based on optical flow.', 'A metric used for solving the matching problem.', 'A method to measure the similarity between poses based on the flow of joints over time.'], 'type': ['method'], 'source_chunk_index': [2, 4]}, 'Person Re-ID': {'description': ['The task of re-identifying individuals across different camera views or time instances.', 'The task of re-identifying a specific person across different camera views or video frames.', 'The task of re-identifying a specific person across different camera views or video frames.', 'The task of re-identifying a person across different camera views or time instances.', 'The task of re-identifying a person across different camera views or time instances.', 'Task for training person Re-ID task.'], 'type': ['task'], 'source_chunk_index': [8, 9, 2, 7]}, 'Flow-based pose similarity as metric': {'description': ['The method used in [50] to solve the matching problem in a greedy fashion, based on flow.', 'A method to measure the similarity between poses based on the flow of joints over time.'], 'type': ['method'], 'source_chunk_index': [2, 4]}, 'Pose Estimation': {'description': ['The task of determining the positions of key body joints (e.g., shoulders, elbows, knees) in an image or video frame.'], 'type': ['task'], 'source_chunk_index': [2, 12]}, 'Scale-normalized image and feature pyramid (SIFP)': {'description': ['A paradigm proposed to address scale variation issues in pose estimation.', 'A paradigm designed to handle scale variations in unified pose approaches.'], 'type': ['method'], 'source_chunk_index': [3, 12]}, 'Computer Vision': {'description': ['The field of computer vision, which encompasses the development of methods for enabling computers to "see" and interpret images, is the application domain for the pose tracking and estimation methods.', 'The field of computer science that enables computers to "see" and interpret images.'], 'type': ['task'], 'source_chunk_index': [3, 5]}, 'Spatiotemporal graph': {'description': ['A graph constructed on the detected joints.', 'A graph structure that represents the relationships between detected joints across both space and time, used for multi-person pose tracking.', 'A graph structure used to represent the relationships between human poses across both space and time, often used in pose tracking.'], 'type': ['generic'], 'source_chunk_index': [4]}, 'Bipartite graph matching problem': {'description': ['A problem solved based on IoU.', 'A method used to find the best matches between two sets of nodes in a graph, often used in pose tracking to match poses across frames.'], 'type': ['method', 'task'], 'source_chunk_index': [4]}, 'Pose flow non maximum suppression (NMS)': {'description': ['A method to eliminate issues like ID switches.', 'A technique used to eliminate ID switches in multi-person pose tracking by constructing pose flow and applying non-maximum suppression to the pose flow.', 'A technique used to eliminate redundant or overlapping pose detections, often used in pose tracking to avoid ID switches.'], 'type': ['method'], 'source_chunk_index': [4]}, 'Energy minimizing function': {'description': ['A mathematical function used to optimize the spatiotemporal graph constructed on the detected joints in multi-person pose tracking, aiming to find the most likely pose configurations over time.', 'A mathematical function that is minimized to find the optimal solution, often used in pose tracking to find the best match between poses over time.'], 'type': ['method'], 'source_chunk_index': [4]}, 'Bipartite graph matching': {'description': ['A method used to solve the problem of associating detected human poses across frames, often based on metrics like IoU (Intersection over Union).', 'A method used to find the best matches between two sets of nodes in a graph, often used in pose tracking to match poses across frames.'], 'type': ['method'], 'source_chunk_index': [4]}, 'Bottom-up Pose Estimation': {'description': ['A method for human pose estimation that first detects individual body parts or joints and then assembles them to form full human poses.', 'A method for human pose estimation that first detects the human bounding boxes and then estimates the pose within each box.'], 'type': ['method'], 'source_chunk_index': [4]}, 'Fast R-CNN': {'description': ['A method used for object detection in images.', 'An improved version of Fast R-CNN, used for object detection.'], 'type': ['method'], 'source_chunk_index': [5]}, 'Scale-normalized image pyramid and feature pyramid (SIFP)': {'description': ['A paradigm exploited to alleviate the scale variation problem of MTN.', 'A paradigm designed to handle scale variations in unified pose approaches.'], 'type': ['method'], 'source_chunk_index': [12, 6]}, 'PoseTrack dataset': {'description': ['A dataset used for evaluating pose estimation and tracking methods.'], 'type': ['dataset'], 'source_chunk_index': [10, 11]}}
